    "title": "Check Whether Two Insertion Sequences Produce the Same Binary Search Tree",
    "category": "Binary Search Trees",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "Given two sequences of distinct keys inserted into initially empty Binary Search Trees, determine whether both insertion sequences produce identical Binary Search Trees without explicitly constructing both trees.",
    "input": "\u2022 The first line contains an integer N. \u2022 The second line contains the first insertion sequence. \u2022 The third line contains the second insertion sequence.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print YES if both sequences generate identical BSTs; otherwise print NO.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 0 \u2264 N \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5"
